CORE
main.c
--show-struct-alignment
^EXIT=0$
^SIGNAL=0$
^WARNING: declaration of structure narrow at file main\.c line 1$
^members a and b might interfere$
^WARNING: declaration of structure pad at file main\.c line 11$
^members c and s might interfere$
--
^warning: ignoring
structure wide
members x and y
\$pad
--
Members that fit in a single memory operand (an int) may interfere, which a and
b do, while x and y do not. The padding between c and s counts towards the
size of the memory operand, but is not reported as a member.
